title: Monetary Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
frequency: 500
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and reichsbank_timer == 0 and reichsbank_seized == 0
card-image: img/Reichsbank.jpg
go-to: @reichsbank_menu

= Monetary Policy

[? if hjalmar_plot != "successful" and year < 1930 and month < 3: Hjalmar Schacht opinion: Hateful. ?]

[? if hjalmar_plot != "successful" and year >= 1930 and month >= 3: Hjalmar Schacht influence: suffocating. ?]

[? if hjalmar_plot == "successful": Now that the Reichsbank is controlled by Hans Luther, perhaps now the Reichsbank will heed our policies.?]

[? if hjalmar_plot == "successful": Hans Luther opinion: [+ hans_opinion : hans_opinion +]. [? if hans_opinion <= 2 : We can persuade him by talking to him directly. ?] ?]

Current devaluation [+ deval_currency_string +]%

Reichsbank reserve requirement: 40%

@reichsbank_menu

- @interest_rates_menu: Interest Rates
- @bonds_menu: Selling Bonds
- @devalue_currency2: Move onto formal devaluation
- @devalue_currency1: Discuss currency devaluation
- @devalue_currency_troll: Discuss currency devaluation
- @bribe: Maybe 1 million Reichsmarks can change his mind.
- @troll: Maybe 1 million Reichsmarks can change his mind.
- @root: No, we're going to our own thing.
- @easy_discard

@interest_rates_menu

- @raise_interest_rates
- @lower_interest_rates_normal
- @lower_interest_rates_very_low
- @reichsbank_menu: Go back.

@raise_interest_rates
title: Increase interest rates
subtitle: Affects middle class and rural much more than workers. [? if interest_rates >= 2 : Interest rates are too high. ?] [? if reichsbank_a != 1 : Hjalmar Schacht would never listen to us. ?]
choose-if: 2 > interest_rates and reichsbank_a == 1 and hans_opinion > 2
on-arrival: currency_value -= 0.05 if interest_rates == -2; inflation -= 1.5 if inflation <= 0; inflation -= 1 if inflation > 0; inflation -= 2 if inflation >= 4; inflation -= 2 if inflation >= 8; unemployed += inflation; workers_spd -= 1; unemployed_spd -= 1; rural_spd -= 1*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 4; capital_strike_progress += 1; interest_rates +=1; economic_growth -= 0.5 if economic_growth <= 0; economic_growth -= 1 if economic_growth > 0; economic_growth -= 1 if economic_growth >= 3; economic_growth -= 2 if economic_growth >= 8; month_actions +=1; hans_opinion -=1 if economic_growth < 3; reichsbank_timer += 4; month_actions += 1

Increasing interest rates decreases inflation, especially if inflation is high. [? if economic_growth < 3: Hans luther reluctanctly agrees, but thinks less of us because he thinks economic growth is too low?]

@lower_interest_rates_normal
title: Decrease interest rates
view-if: interest_rates >= 0
subtitle: Affects middle class and rural much more than workers [? if interest_rates <= -2 : Interest rates are too low. ?] [? if reichsbank_a != 1 : Hjalmar Schacht would never listen to us. ?]
choose-if: interest_rates > -2 and reichsbank_a == 1 and hans_opinion > 2
on-arrival: inflation += 1.5 if inflation <= 0; inflation += 1 if inflation > 0; inflation += 1 if inflation >= 4; inflation += 1 if inflation >= 8; workers_spd += 1; unemployed_spd += 1; rural_spd += 1*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 4; capital_strike_progress -= 1; interest_rates -=1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 0; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth > 0; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth >= 3; economic_growth += 2 if economic_growth >= 8; month_actions +=1; hans_opinion -= 1 if inflation >= 5; reichsbank_timer += 4; month_actions += 1

Decreasing interest rates stimulates economic growth, but increases inflation. [? if inflation >= 5: Hans luther reluctanctly agrees, but thinks less of us because he thinks inflation is too high?]

@lower_interest_rates_very_low
title: Decrease interest rates
view-if: interest_rates < 0
subtitle: Affects middle class and rural much more than workers. [? if interest_rates <= -2 : Interest rates are far too low. ?] [? if reichsbank_a != 1 : Hjalmar Schacht would never listen to us. ?] [? if devaluation_stage <= 0 : Lowering Interest rates would force currency devaluation, which both party and Reichsbank detests. ?]
choose-if: interest_rates > -2 and reichsbank_a == 1 and hans_opinion > 2 and devaluation_stage == 1
on-arrival: inflation += 1 if inflation <= 0; inflation += 0.5 if inflation > 0; inflation += 0.5 if inflation >= 4; inflation += 0.5 if inflation >= 8; workers_spd += 1; unemployed_spd += 1; rural_spd += 1*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 4; capital_strike_progress -= 1; interest_rates -=1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 0; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth > 0; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth >= 3; economic_growth += 2 if economic_growth >= 8; month_actions +=1; hans_opinion -= 1 if inflation >= 5; reichsbank_timer += 4; month_actions += 1; currency_value += 0.05

Decreasing interest rates stimulates economic growth, but increases inflation. [? if inflation >= 5: Hans luther reluctanctly agrees, but thinks less of us because he thinks inflation is too high?]

@bonds_menu
choose-if: devaluation_stage >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot devalue our currency

Instead of citizens buying our bonds, the Reichsbank could buy them instead, affecting our currency exchange rate.

- @issue_bond_1: Issue a small number of bonds.
- @issue_bond_2: Issue a sizeable number of bonds.
- @issue_bond_3: Issue a large number of bonds
- @reichsbank_menu: Go back.
- @easy_discard

@issue_bond_1
subtitle: +1 budget, with interest
unavailable-subtitle: Wait for [+ bond_timer +] months.
choose-if: bond_timer == 0
on-arrival: budget +=1; bond_timer = 12; currency_value +=0.02; {!
Q.list_debt_date.push(4); Q.list_debt_amount.push(1)
!}

We have to pay this back at 30% interest rate per year, for 4 years. if we go into deficit spending in this, we *can* have the option to default, this is not recommended.

@issue_bond_2
subtitle: +2 budget, with interest
unavailable-subtitle: Wait for [+ bond_timer +] months.
choose-if: bond_timer == 0
on-arrival: budget +=2; bond_timer = 12; currency_value +=0.04; {!
Q.list_debt_date.push(4); Q.list_debt_amount.push(2)
!}

We have to pay this back at 30% interest rate per year, for 4 years. if we go into deficit spending in this, we *can* have the option to default, this is not recommended.

@issue_bond_3
subtitle: +3 budget, with interest
unavailable-subtitle: Wait for [+ bond_timer +] months.
choose-if: bond_timer == 0
on-arrival: budget +=3; bond_timer = 12; currency_value +=0.06; {!
Q.list_debt_date.push(4); Q.list_debt_amount.push(3)
!}

We have to pay this back at 30% interest rate per year, for 4 years. if we go into deficit spending in this, we *can* have the option to default, this is not recommended.

@pegging_menu
title: Peg the Reichsmark to gold
choose-if: devaluation_stage >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot formally devalue our currency

- @peg_higher: peg higher (5%)
- @peg_lower: peg lower (5%)

@peg_higher
on-arrival: currency_value -=0.05

We increased the reichsmark to gold ratio.

@peg_lower
on-arrival: currency_value +=0.05

We decreased the reichsmark to gold ratio.

@bribe
view-if: reichsbank_a == 1 and hans_opinion <= 2
title: With hans being uncooperative, perhaps he needs an "incentive".
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources > 0
on-arrival: hans_opinion +=1; resources -=1; barmat +=1 if barmat <= 2; reichsbank_timer += 4; month_actions += 1

By transferring our funds in Hans Luther's wallet, he may think more highly of us.

@troll
view-if: reichsbank_a == 0
title: Perhaps he needs an, "incentive"
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources > 0
on-arrival: resources -=1; barmat +=1 if barmat <= 2; reichsbank_timer += 4; month_actions += 1

No it did not.


@devalue_currency1
view-if: devaluation_stage == 0
choose-if: devaluation_progress >= 3 and hjalmar_plot == "successful"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if devaluation_progress < 3 : Devaluation has little support within the party. ?] [? if hjalmar_plot != "successful" : Schacht would never allow this. ?]
on-arrival: devaluation_stage = 1; currency_value_cap = 1.15

After talks within our party, and Hans Luther, he has agreed to do some policies of monetary devaluation. Such as further reducing interest rates, and buying government bonds.
Note, that Hans Luther has only agreed to this on the condition that the maximum amount of devaluation we do do is 15%.

@devalue_currency_troll
max-visits: 1

Hilderfing, surprisingly on board with currency devaluation, goes up to Schacht to discuss plans to do this.

Schacht, horrified of what Hilderfing uttered, hit him in the head with a hammer multiple times!

After the horrifying ordeal, Hilderfing has, surprisingly, came unscathed, except for returning back into his economic orthodoxy of doing nothing. 

<iframe src="https://giphy.com/embed/MaUXRiSomZXMiouCc0" width="480" height="432" style="" frameBorder="0" class="giphy-embed" allowFullScreen></iframe><p><a href="https://giphy.com/gifs/Clash-Royale-MaUXRiSomZXMiouCc0">via GIPHY</a></p>

@devalue_currency2
view-if: devaluation_stage == 1
choose-if: devaluation_progress >= 6 and hjalmar_plot == "successful" and allies_allow_devaluation
unavailable-subtitle: [? if allies_allow_devaluation != 1 : The allies would never allow this, without further negotiations. ?]
on-arrival: devaluation_stage = 2; currency_value_cap = 1.3


After or successful policies of devaluation, our party and Hans Luther, has agreed to do formal monetary devaluation. Which means pegging the Reichsmark to a higher or lower amount to gold. He has also agreed to a higher set limit of devaluation at 30%, instead of the previous 15%.